        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Question 1",
            "id": 75856,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the keyword that decides if a code block should run or not?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>if</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>when</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>for</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>if</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A game should show a message only when <code>game_over</code> is <code>True</code>. Which line should start that check?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>if game_over:</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>when game_over:</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>for game_over:</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>if game_over:</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example 5",
            "id": 75894,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code the variable that displays <code>\"Take an umbrella\"</code> in the console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"is_rainy = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"is_sunny = \" /><text value=\"False\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" is_rainy:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Take an umbrella&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"36\" endIndex=\"44\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"is_sunny\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Take an umbrella\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>is_rainy</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Set <code>is_rainy</code> so its block runs. Use that variable as the condition to print <code>Take an umbrella</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"is_rainy = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"is_sunny = \" /><text value=\"False\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" is_rainy:\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Take an umbrella&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"36\" endIndex=\"44\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"15\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"is_sunny\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"False\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Take an umbrella\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>True</code>, followed by <code>is_rainy</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 6",
            "id": 75863,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What kind of value do we use as a condition for an if statement?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Boolean</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">String</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Number</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick Boolean.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You can use a stored boolean as a condition for an <code>if</code> statement.</p><p>The variable <code>is_open</code> stores <code>False</code>. Which expression gives that stored boolean value?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>is_open</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>\"is_open\"</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>0</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>is_open</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 5",
            "id": 75864,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Based on indentation, when will <code>print(\"Starting game ...\")</code> run?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"character = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Wizard&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" character == \" /><text value=\"&quot;Knight&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\": \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Weapon: sword&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Starting game ...&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Always, regardless of whether the <code>if</code> block runs, as it's indented at the same level</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Only when the <code>if</code> block runs</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Never, because this code gives an <code>IndentationError</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Always, regardless of whether the <code>if</code> block runs, as it's indented at the same level.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>You run this code with <code>character</code> set to <code>\"Wizard\"</code>. What does it display?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"character = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Wizard&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" character == \" /><text value=\"&quot;Knight&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\": \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Weapon: sword&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Starting game ...&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Only <code>Starting game ...</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>Weapon: sword</code>, then <code>Starting game ...</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Nothing, because the condition is <code>False</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Only <code>Starting game ...</code></p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 4",
            "id": 75858,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What do we call statements that run or skip code depending on a condition being <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">If statements</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Else statements</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">For loops</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">If statements.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>is_member</code> stores <code>False</code>. What does <code>if is_member:</code> do with its indented welcome message?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It skips the welcome message.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It prints the welcome message because is_member exists.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">It prints False instead of the welcome message.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It skips the welcome message.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Correct answers",
            "id": 76588,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code display?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"name = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" name == \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Hi Sue!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Hi Sue!\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>Hi Sue!</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Nothing, the condition is <code>False</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>Sue</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>Hi Sue!</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why does this code display <code>Hi Sue!</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"name = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" name == \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Hi Sue!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Hi Sue!\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The comparison is <code>True</code>, so the indented <code>print()</code> runs.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The comparison changes <code>name</code> to <code>\"Sue\"</code>.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The <code>print()</code> runs regardless of the condition because it is outside the block.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The comparison is <code>True</code>, so the indented <code>print()</code> runs.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Condition",
            "id": 76566,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code display?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"weather = \" /><text value=\"&quot;rainy&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"color_code = \" /><text value=\"&quot;yellow&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" weather == \" /><text value=\"&quot;rainy&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color_code = \" /><text value=\"&quot;blue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(color_code)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"blue\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>blue</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>yellow</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>color_code</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>blue</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why does this code display <code>blue</code> instead of <code>yellow</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"weather = \" /><text value=\"&quot;rainy&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"color_code = \" /><text value=\"&quot;yellow&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" weather == \" /><text value=\"&quot;rainy&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color_code = \" /><text value=\"&quot;blue&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(color_code)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"blue\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The condition is <code>True</code>, so <code>color_code</code> changes before it is printed.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The condition is <code>False</code>, so <code>color_code</code> keeps its first value.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>print()</code> displays the variable name instead of its current value.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The condition is <code>True</code>, so <code>color_code</code> changes before it is printed.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Wrong answers",
            "id": 76544,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code a condition that runs the display statement only if <code>character</code> is <em>not</em> equal to <code>\"Wizard\"</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"character = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Wizard&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" character != \" /><text value=\"&quot;Wizard&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\": \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;You can't use spells&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option startIndex=\"35\" endIndex=\"37\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>character</code>, followed by <code>!=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The block should run only when <code>character</code> is <em>not</em> <code>\"Wizard\"</code>. Build that check so this run, where it <em>is</em> <code>\"Wizard\"</code>, prints nothing.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"character = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Wizard&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" character != \" /><text value=\"&quot;Wizard&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\": \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;You can't use spells&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"25\" endIndex=\"34\" /><option startIndex=\"35\" endIndex=\"37\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"=\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>character</code>, followed by <code>!=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Correct answers",
            "id": 76553,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code an operator to make the condition <code>True</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"account = \" /><text value=\"&quot;premium&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" account == \" /><text value=\"&quot;premium&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\": \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Exclude from data set&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"31\" endIndex=\"33\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Exclude from data set\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Good decisions",
            "id": 76564,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why are comparisons better conditions than just <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Because the value of variables can change, so it may run or skip a code block depending on the value</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We can't use comparison as conditions</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Because they are always <code>True</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Because the value of variables can change, so it may run or skip a code block depending on the value.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A weather app should show a warning only when <code>temperature &gt; 30</code>. Why use that comparison as the condition instead of <code>True</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Its result can change with <code>temperature</code>, so the warning can run or be skipped.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A comparison prevents the warning code from ever running.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">A comparison always produces <code>True</code>.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Its result can change with <code>temperature</code>, so the warning can run or be skipped.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
